    {
      "run": 1,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "I started my expedition in this damp, salted galley, a relic of a bygone era. The compact space was littered with remnants of nautical life, but my focus was solely on a seemingly ordinary kettle lying on the floor. Ignoring the corroded ambiance and the rusty footprints of sailors past, I picked up the kettle, drawn to its potential utility. Upon closer inspection, I found it to be a hardy, tin vessel, marred by age, particularly on one side, as if it had seen its fair share of stormy seas. Despite my attempt to open it, it remained stubbornly closed, a reminder of its weathered state. Now, holding the kettle tightly, I ponder my next step, considering the northward passage and the southward descent through the hatch beneath my feet.",
