      "narrative": "Having descended the hatch, I found myself in a dimly lit area under the galley. I had the impression of being in a small, cramped space, much like the galley above, but with a distinct under-deck feel to it. The air was damp and had a faint metallic scent, suggestive of the ship's guts. The only thing I had taken with me was the kettle, its metal surface cool and smooth in my hand. I had hoped to find some sort of entrance or passage leading further into the ship, perhaps to the lower decks or even the engine room. However, my exploration was cut short as I realized my movements were causing unreasonable requests, the narrative unable to process my commands effectively.",
