      "run": 5,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "In the cramped, salty galley, I noticed a kettle lying on the floor and decided to take it. Examining the kettle, I observed it was old and dented, but functional. I then opened the hatch leading downwards and descended into the chilly, low-lying cistern. This area was devoid of visible water sources, but I found a rusted tin cup. I managed to pour water from the kettle into the cup, aiming to make use of the makeshift vessel. However, in my attempt to describe this sequence of events, I encountered difficulties in formulating the actions in appropriate terms. Despite this, I remained determined to document my experience in this unfamiliar, yet intriguing environment.",
